      "abstract": [
        {
          "identifier": "abstract",
          "language": "en",
          "value": "An alignment ontology describing artificial intelligence applications in automated plants together with the plant and the technical process it runs. It imports three subdomain patterns, for the technical process after VDI/VDE 3682, for communication after ISO/IEC 7498-1 and for artificial intelligence after ISO/IEC 22989, and ties them together through three collecting classes: a function, a component and a relation. Placing a process operator and an inference under one function class is what makes them comparable, so that the same assignment states which resource carries out which function, whichever subdomain that function comes from. Twelve own classes and eight own relations. Nothing here is normative: the patterns rest on standards, the alignment rests on design decisions.",
          "type": "label"
        }
      ],
